{
  "id": "guqf5xp",
  "title": "Solved Examples – Number System",
  "order": 3,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "8wnudaq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Example 1: Find the number of factors of 72."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Chapter Focus",
          "value": "Number System",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Total Factors of 72",
          "value": "12",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "HCF of 24 & 36",
          "value": "12",
          "icon": "award"
        }
      ],
      "id": "xktgcb3"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "To calculate the total number of factors of a number, express it in prime factorized form a^p × b^q and multiply the incremented exponents: (p+1)(q+1).",
        "Prime factorization of 72 is 2^3 × 3^2, giving (3+1)(2+1) = 12 total factors.",
        "The Highest Common Factor (HCF) is determined by taking the product of the smallest powers of each common prime factor.",
        "The prime factors of 24 are 2^3 × 3 and for 36 are 2^2 × 3^2, making their HCF 2^2 × 3 = 12."
      ],
      "id": "8ptxlv1"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jildjws",
      "content": "Step 1: Perform prime factorization. 72 = 2 × 2 × 2 × 3 × 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ar02343",
      "content": "72 = 2³ × 3²"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8dsry2k",
      "content": "Step 2: Use the formula for number of factors. If N = pᵃ × qᵇ,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0p0q291",
      "content": "Number of factors = (a + 1)(b + 1) Here, a = 3 and b = 2."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i3d49mw",
      "content": "Number of factors = (3 + 1)(2 + 1)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "qtcwxs2",
      "content": "= 4 × 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "j5ova6o",
      "content": "= 12"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mctnyrn",
      "content": "Final Answer: 72 has 12 factors."
    },
    {
      "id": "olyokzl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Example 2: Find the HCF of 24 and 36."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jfczmej",
      "content": "Step 1: Prime factorize both numbers. 24 = 2 × 2 × 2 × 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "hmrvc3z",
      "content": "24 = 2³ × 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a5fgiag",
      "content": "36 = 2 × 2 × 3 × 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "nqiqllk",
      "content": "36 = 2² × 3²"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "48af7dr",
      "content": "Step 2: Identify the common prime factors with the smallest powers. Common factor of 2 → minimum power is 2&lt;"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8oemd0y",
      "content": "Common factor of 3 → minimum power is 3¹ Step 3: Multiply them."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "3oxijy9",
      "content": "HCF = 2² × 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "80oq07h",
      "content": "= 4 × 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "wtf92tm",
      "content": "= 12"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "atjsjdr",
      "content": "Final Answer: The HCF of 24 and 36 is 12."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m9i6tvi",
      "content": "<strong>Example 3: Find the unit digit of 9^23. </strong>Step 1: Observe the unit digit pattern of powers of 9. 9; = 9 → Unit digit = 9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "npdpi8a",
      "content": "9&lt; = 81 → Unit digit = 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cfczvd8",
      "content": "9= = 729 → Unit digit = 9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u2k84g1",
      "content": "9&gt; = 6561 → Unit digit = 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "eb0slqi",
      "content": "The unit digits repeat in a cycle: 9, 1. Cycle length = 2."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g8xnrot",
      "content": "Step 2: Divide the exponent by the cycle length. 23"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "btm7zl4",
      "content": "÷ 2 leaves a remainder of 1."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fejm1v1",
      "content": "Step 3: Match the remainder with the cycle."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Find the number of factors of 72.",
      "id": "5rjdczv"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u17itgg",
      "content": "Remainder 1 corresponds to the first number in the cycle → 9. Final Answer: The unit digit of 9^23 is 9."
    },
    {
      "id": "hnb57cp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Practice Questions with Solutions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f2zpnr0",
      "content": "<strong>Question 1</strong>: Find the LCM of 16 and 20."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "chqknn2",
      "content": "Step 1: Perform prime factorization of both numbers. 16 = 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 = 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mp4mxo1",
      "content": "20 = 2 × 2 × 5 = 2² × 5"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d05s949",
      "content": "Step 2: Identify the highest power of each prime factor. Highest power of 2 → 2⁴"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "70ex4da",
      "content": "Highest power of 5 → 5;"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bv9ssu6",
      "content": "Step 3: Multiply them to obtain the LCM. LCM = 2&gt; × 5"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "4b4unsr",
      "content": "= 16 × 5"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ere4kt8",
      "content": "= 80"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vanzm1c",
      "content": "Final Answer: The LCM of 16 and 20 is 80."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lf4k7p6",
      "content": "<strong>Question 2</strong>: How many factors does 100 have? Step 1: Prime factorize the number."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ijnl31n",
      "content": "100 = 2 × 2 × 5 × 5"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "knkm0au",
      "content": "100 = 2² × 5²"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lw0byp2",
      "content": "Step 2: Use the formula for counting factors."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "idi81v1",
      "content": "If N = pᵃ × qᵇ,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "771zwgk",
      "content": "Number of factors = (a + 1)(b + 1) Here, a = 2 and b = 2."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hq5irop",
      "content": "Number of factors = (2 + 1)(2 + 1)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "dlywmzd",
      "content": "=&gt; 3 × 3= 9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yq00543",
      "content": "Final Answer: 100 has 9 factors."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7ut7pxc",
      "content": "<strong>Question 3</strong>: Find the remainder when 3⁷ is divided by 4. Step 1: Reduce the base using modulus."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y3roi6k",
      "content": "3 ÷ 4 leaves remainder 3."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g3t59n4",
      "content": "So, 3 ≡ -1 (mod 4)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x9cdvk0",
      "content": "Step 2: Rewrite the expression."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "echlykz",
      "content": "3⁷ ≡ (-1)⁷ (mod 4)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t5hy4wq",
      "content": "Step 3: Evaluate the power. (-1)⁷ = -1"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "618q931",
      "content": "Step 4: Convert the negative remainder into a positive remainder."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "0me9ba5",
      "content": "-1 mod 4 = 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "epncuva",
      "content": "Final Answer: The remainder is 3."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2w7tfiv",
      "content": "<strong>Question 4</strong>: Is 121 a perfect square?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6gfo7yu",
      "content": "Step 1: Find the square root of the number."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "g4qbj3d",
      "content": "√121 = 11"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iugyb5s",
      "content": "Step 2: Check whether the square root is an integer. Since 11 is a whole number and 11× 11 = 121, 121 is a perfect square."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ch1o498",
      "content": "Final Answer: Yes, 121 is a perfect square."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Always prime factorize a number completely before applying the total factors formula (p+1)(q+1)(r+1).",
        "HCF and LCM concepts are fundamental high-frequency topics in SSC CGL, RRB NTPC, and UPSC CSAT quantitative aptitude sections."
      ],
      "id": "gvfzm30"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "offt6vn",
      "content": "<strong>Question 5</strong>: Convert (1101)₂ into decimal. Step 1: Write the place values for base 2. From right to left:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "heywkjt",
      "content": "2º, 2<sup>2</sup>, 2<sup>3</sup>, 2<sup>4</sup>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uqb8xs6",
      "content": "Step 2: Multiply each digit by its place value. 1 × 2³ = 8"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "rlubt1g",
      "content": "1 × 2² = 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "bzlcxiw",
      "content": "0 × 2¹ = 0"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "kbfvkhp",
      "content": "1 × 2º = 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qkanqni",
      "content": "Step 3: Add the results."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ekh9azc",
      "content": "8 + 4 + 0 + 1 = 13"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6s6v4h0",
      "content": "Final Answer: (1101)₂ = 13 in decimal."
    },
    {
      "id": "i4nj654",
